# Clockify time (from .clockify.yml)

This workspace tracks time in Clockify workspace **GitHub**, project **career-pipeline**. Credentials live in local `.env` (`CLOCKIFY_WORKSPACE_ID`). Use Clockify MCP tools only; never invent project or task ids.

Align with the git workflow: one issue per concern; one issue per PR. Map the issue’s primary type label (`feat` / `fix` / `docs` / `chore` / `refactor` / `sec` / `breaking`) to the matching Clockify task when starting a timer.

## Triggers

| Moment | Action |
|--------|--------|
| Start work or planning on a GitHub issue | `clockify_start_timer` with `issue_number` + `issue_title` (and `github_label` when known) |
| Finish the issue in this session | `clockify_stop_timer` |
| Switch issues | stop, then start for the new issue |
| Ship the PR in this session (`pr_ship`) | `clockify_stop_timer` |
| Session start / resume | `clockify_get_running_timer`; if inactivity is past threshold (45m), stop or ask |

Rounding (nearest 15 minutes) comes from `.clockify.yml` when stopping.

## Do not

- Claim timers stop on GitHub merge without an agent (that needs a phase-2 GitHub Action)
- Put API keys in rules or `.clockify.yml`
